      },
      "text": "**A typeface is a frozen voice.** When you read text set in Garamond, you are reading with the proportions that Claude Garamond cut in steel in the 1530s. When you read Times New Roman, you are reading with the proportions Stanley Morison specified for The Times of London in 1932 to maximize column density on newsprint."
